00:03:13.064 --> 00:03:13.897
(audience laughs)

00:03:13.897 --> 00:03:14.810
- Well, I'll put on my imagination hat.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.090
- When you split up with your boyfriend

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.753
and the sex was exceptional,

00:03:17.753 --> 00:03:19.970
but that's all you, all you
we're going out with him for.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:20.803
- Okay, yes.

00:03:20.803 --> 00:03:21.800
- And you split up, and
say we'll just do it,

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.193
well upstairs one more time.

00:03:23.193 --> 00:03:24.135
- Oh.

00:03:24.135 --> 00:03:24.968
(audience cheering)

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.360
This is a great idea.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.420
This is a great idea
for a song, that's real.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:31.560
You're like, I was there
for this, but yeah.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.393
- Yeah.

00:03:32.393 --> 00:03:33.226
- And then it's kind of fun,

00:03:33.226 --> 00:03:34.800
then it's like the red
button like you shouldn't do.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:35.666
- Yeah, shouldn't do it.

00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:36.499
I've never done it myself.

00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:37.332
Have you?

00:03:37.332 --> 00:03:38.321
- Liar. (laughs)

00:03:38.321 --> 00:03:41.032
- On Simon, I have never done it.

00:03:41.032 --> 00:03:41.865
- I've never done it.

00:03:41.865 --> 00:03:44.016
- Just like one more,
you know, (indistinct)

00:03:44.016 --> 00:03:46.099
(laughs)

00:03:47.656 --> 00:03:51.240
- Wait, that was amazing,
I want it to be a GIF.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.040
There's a special song
on the album, though,

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.445
and it's called Touchline.

00:03:54.445 --> 00:03:55.278
- Yeah.

00:03:55.278 --> 00:03:56.460
- So what's, what's this about?

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.290
- Well, I've played soccer-
football all my life

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.400
and I was a pro once,

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.947
but cut a long story short, my dad,

00:04:02.947 --> 00:04:05.490
where there were three of us, three sons.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:06.323
- Yeah.

00:04:06.323 --> 00:04:07.540
- And we all played football
and he was the manager

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:10.090
of the team and he was a
good player in his day too.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:12.805
So he managed the team and
that's in there, it's amazing.

00:04:12.805 --> 00:04:13.638
- Yeah.

00:04:13.638 --> 00:04:15.960
- Long time ago, and he'd
pick the team and he'd

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.680
always be on the touchline,
pouring the rain,

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:22.690
snow, shouting at us, abuse
and everything like that.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.220
And we loved him for it, you know,

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.228
but then of course he passed on.

00:04:26.228 --> 00:04:27.061
- Yeah.

00:04:27.061 --> 00:04:29.980
- And the song's all
about how I find myself

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.150
doing the same thing with my boys.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.988
On the touchline, watching
my sons playing football.

00:04:34.988 --> 00:04:35.821
- I love that.

00:04:35.821 --> 00:04:36.870
- And hopefully, when I'm gone,

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.060
they'll do exactly the
same with their sons.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:43.280
So it's a very, it's a
manly sort of, sort of song.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.220
- Well, and it's cool though,

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.600
because not all men show up
for games for their kids.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:47.730
- Yeah absolutely.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.630
- That's amazing.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.540
- And I think we call it the sideline.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:51.560
So it's the touchline?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.200
- Yeah, touchline in football,
sideline is in your football.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.110
- Okay, okay, right on.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:55.943
Well, that's all,

00:04:55.943 --> 00:04:57.760
that's about all I know about
sports ball, right there.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:58.593
- That's okay, darling.

00:04:58.593 --> 00:04:59.426
- (laughs) Sideline.

00:04:59.426 --> 00:05:00.259
- Let's move on quickly.

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:01.970
- Let's move on quickly. (laughs)

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:03.780
You are loving this interview, okay.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.701
So this year marks the 50th
anniversary of Rod's album

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:08.780
Every Picture Tells a Story,
(audience member cheers)

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.470
which- okay, yes ma'am.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:11.420
(audience cheers)

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.950
You got a grown.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:16.030
It tells a story which
features the hit, Maggie May,

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:18.510
which everyone knows, now
I love that song so much.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.272
It's an amazing album,
obviously you got some fans.

00:05:20.272 --> 00:05:22.890
But I do want to talk
about a favorite of mine.

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.470
And this is not, I told you in the break,

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.340
this is, I'm on tour.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.173
You know, you're always on tour

00:05:26.173 --> 00:05:27.180
and you're in different cities, right?

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.349
Well, I was in Seattle,

00:05:29.349 --> 00:05:30.182
(audience member cheers)

00:05:30.182 --> 00:05:31.370
and they usually have really
great record stores there,

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.130
like vinyl and I've always loved vinyl.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:33.963
Like, since I was a kid,

00:05:33.963 --> 00:05:35.310
it's like the one thing that
was passed down to me in my

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.590
family from my grandmother.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:37.560
So I love vinyl.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.140
And I was in this store and I found,

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.290
It's Never a Dull
Moment, it's your record.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.230
And I think it's from like
the seventies, but it had,

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.770
I noticed and why I picked
it up, I was like, ooh,

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.610
I love Rod Stewart, and then
I was like, oh he covered

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.110
I'd Rather Go Blind, I love that song.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:52.044
And then it turns out it's
literally one of my favorite

00:05:52.044 --> 00:05:54.780
covers of any song that
anyone's ever done.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.110
Not just your voice, the production,

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:58.340
like whoever put that to-

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:01.480
it is so tasteful and so beautiful.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.460
And I'm wondering, 'cause
it wasn't like full of them.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.120
So why did you pick that
song for that record?

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.610
- Well,

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:08.760
Etta James did it first.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.660
- Yes, yeah.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.560
- And then the girl out
Fleetwood Mac did it,

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.310
but it wasn't a big hit.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.930
What's her name, Stevie, not
Stevie Nicks, the other one.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:17.768
- I do know Stevie Nicks-
oh you mean (stammering)

00:06:17.768 --> 00:06:18.601
- The other one.

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:19.434
- She wrote Songbird.

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:20.267
Yep, I'm Blanking.

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:21.200
- Yeah me too, anybody know?

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.328
Not Stevie, the other girl.

00:06:22.328 --> 00:06:23.256
- [Audience] Christine.

00:06:23.256 --> 00:06:24.089
- Christine!

00:06:24.089 --> 00:06:24.922
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:06:24.922 --> 00:06:26.270
- Christine McVie, she did
it and I heard her do it.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:27.283
So I decided to do it.

00:06:27.283 --> 00:06:28.116
- Yeah.

00:06:28.116 --> 00:06:29.280
- But- and it was an after thought,

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.000
I was in the studio with
Ronnie Wood, you know,

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.505
Ronnie is (indistinct) with The Stones.

00:06:32.505 --> 00:06:34.280
And we had nothing to do.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.650
And we said, let's have
a go at Rather Go Blind.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.363
We had three bottles of wine
and we did it in two takes.

00:06:39.363 --> 00:06:40.196
(audience laughs)

00:06:40.196 --> 00:06:41.185
- Okay, I was-.

00:06:41.185 --> 00:06:42.018
- Two takes.

00:06:42.018 --> 00:06:43.134
- I was literally gonna
ask you if that's what-

00:06:43.134 --> 00:06:43.967
(audience claps)

00:06:43.967 --> 00:06:46.550
I feel like, the two things
I love for my career,

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.526
it was literally just like so easy.

00:06:48.526 --> 00:06:49.359
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:49.359 --> 00:06:50.192
It flowed so easy.

00:06:50.192 --> 00:06:51.509
- Like, we didn't work at
it, it wasn't over-produced.

00:06:51.509 --> 00:06:52.342
- Yeah.

00:06:52.342 --> 00:06:53.175
- And it was just like the moment.

00:06:53.175 --> 00:06:54.024
That's what it sounds like.

00:06:54.024 --> 00:06:54.857
- Yeah, that how it was.

00:06:54.857 --> 00:06:55.690
- Yeah.

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:56.760
- People love it.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.740
- So lesson learned, I just got
to have two bottles of wine,

00:06:58.740 --> 00:06:59.620
and record some music (audience laughs)

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:00.830
and it'll be magical.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:03.920
So is it true that you and
Ronnie are back in the studio?

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:04.930
You were just talking about Ronnie Woods,

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:05.763
so are y'all back in?

00:07:05.763 --> 00:07:06.596
- Yeah, yeah.

00:07:06.596 --> 00:07:09.530
Ronnie has been spending
a lot of time digging up

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.310
a lot of old Faces stuff
from the early seventies.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:13.143
- Yeah.

00:07:13.143 --> 00:07:14.190
- And we were putting
it all back together.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:16.050
It was about 60 odd tracks.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:16.976
- Wow.

00:07:16.976 --> 00:07:17.809
- And I said, Ronnie, don't sing,

00:07:17.809 --> 00:07:20.510
I can't sing in the same key, you know.

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:21.343
- Change the key.

00:07:21.343 --> 00:07:23.350
- We, well I suppose we could.

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:24.710
Yeah, but that'd be cheating, wouldn't it?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.543
- No.

00:07:25.543 --> 00:07:26.660
- Because you have to rerecord it again.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.150
